On 2026-08-30, this repository intentionally modified the vendored `punk-cover`
`SKILL.md` and `references/cover-prompt-blueprint.md`. The local adaptation
distinguishes source facts, user-authored copy, and unapproved suggestions;
requires actual-artifact text inspection; and adds deterministic typography,
explicit validation statuses, bounded retries, narrow cover-only discovery,
and explicit style-selection delegation. Standalone posters, flyers, key
visuals, and generic poster prompts route directly to `punk-poster-layout` when
they explicitly need structural composition control. Article, social, and
platform covers remain with `punk-cover` even with poster-like treatment; when
they explicitly request focal flow, grids, image-text relationships, or density,
`punk-poster-layout` serves only as a subordinate structural step.
Style delegation selects exactly one eligible catalog style but never approves
model-derived visible copy. The change also prevents an image model's
generated, misspelled, missing, or cropped text from being reported as verified
merely because the prompt contained the intended copy. Matching modification
notices are included at the `punk-cover` plugin root and skill root.

